The event data model layer with libc++ and on macOS:
- TrkExUtils, TrkPatternParameters: __sincos() on macOS, where sincos() (a GNU extension) is
  missing;
- includes that libstdc++ brings in through other headers and libc++ does not (<sstream>,
  <algorithm>), and no <malloc.h> where nothing from it is used;
- NavFourMom: no second definition of DVLEltBaseInit<T>::s_regbase for macOS (an old linker
  workaround: AthContainers defines it, as const, and clang rejects the mismatch);
- PyDumper: the compiler's __BYTE_ORDER__ rather than glibc's __BYTE_ORDER (undefined on macOS,
  where both bit field layouts were declared).

--- a/Tracking/TrkExtrapolation/TrkExUtils/src/RungeKuttaUtils.cxx
+++ b/Tracking/TrkExtrapolation/TrkExUtils/src/RungeKuttaUtils.cxx
@@ -19,6 +19,13 @@
 
 #include "CxxUtils/vec.h"
 #include "CxxUtils/inline_hints.h"
+
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+namespace {
+// sincos() is a GNU extension; macOS has __sincos()
+inline void sincos(double x, double* s, double* c) { __sincos(x, s, c); }
+}
+#endif
 
